course: dictionary
lesson: 10356
title: Words that carry things
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A transporter is something that carries things from one place to another. The word comes from transport, which means to carry, and the ending -er means the thing that does the carrying. Breaking a word into parts can help you work out its meaning.
explain: «New cars travel to dealers on double-deck car transporter lorries.» The clue is car. A car transporter is a lorry built to carry cars, so you can work out the meaning from the words around it.
explain: Read on and you may find transporter used in other ways. In science fiction, a transporter is an imaginary machine that sends people instantly from one place to another. In science, a transporter is a tiny part of a cell that carries substances in or out. Each meaning still involves carrying something from place to place.
fact: A transporter is a large vehicle that carries other vehicles or heavy loads.
fact: A transporter can also be any person or thing that carries something from place to place.
fact: A car transporter is a lorry that carries cars.
fact: In science fiction, a transporter is an imaginary machine that sends people instantly from one place to another.
fact: Transporter proteins are tiny parts of a cell that move substances in and out.
exercise: «New cars travel to dealers on double-deck car transporter lorries.» What is a car transporter lorry? | A ship that carries people | A small car with two decks | *A large lorry that carries cars | A shop that sells cars
exercise: Which word describes an imaginary machine that sends people instantly from one place to another? | A bridge | *A transporter | A lorry | A tractor
exercise: Find and copy the word in «New cars travel to dealers on double-deck car transporter lorries» that tells you what the transporter carries. | *car | dealers | travel | double-deck
test: Which is the best meaning of transporter? | A kind of road sign | A type of cell that never moves | *A large vehicle or thing that carries things from place to place | A shop for buying cars
test: In science, what does a transporter protein do? | Sends people to other planets | Builds walls around the cell | Makes the cell grow taller | *Moves substances in and out of a cell
exam: Using the clue car, what does transporter mean in «car transporter lorries»? | A road with no cars on it | Something that is painted red | A driver who sells cars all day | *A vehicle that carries cars
